WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.400
The internal assembly and manifold organize equipment and fluid connections, but their

2
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:05.380
roles are distinct.

3
00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:09.260
Mechanical support establishes reference positions and permitted movement.

4
00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:12.460
The manifold distributes coolant through a defined arrangement.

5
00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:16.140
The coupling must work within the relationship those assemblies create.

6
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.860
Review alignment and deflection across the complete tolerance chain, not only at

7
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:21.960
an isolated connection.

8
00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:25.380
Then include the space needed for installation and service.

9
00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:29.820
A support arrangement can be structurally acceptable while placing a connection outside

10
00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:31.040
its permitted mating condition.

11
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:35.760
The source-derived plate shows the relevant parts without inventing an internal mechanism.

12
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:39.840
Use the controlling drawings and supplier requirements when geometry matters.

13
00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:44.040
Check that cable and hose routing doesn't impose unintended loads or obstruct

14
00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:44.480
movement.

15
00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:48.360
The resulting review should establish that the configured equipment can be supported,

16
00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:52.880
connected and serviced under its qualified conditions, rather than assuming a common

17
00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.420
assembly name guarantees every interface around it.

